\section{Discussion}
\label{sec:discussion}

Symbolic confirmation bias unifies two degradation channels: the \emph{direct} channel limits voting diversity (Eff-$K < 2$), while the \emph{indirect} channel causes MAX-SAT to degenerate to vote counting. The cross-architecture NLI experiment (\S\ref{sec:cross-arch}) corroborates that complementary signal must come from outside the model's distribution. For practitioners, $C_0$ combined with SC accuracy predicts when augmentation is unlikely to help: $C_0 < 5\%$ implies degeneration, SC $\geq 60\%$ implies confirmation bias, SC $\leq 40\%$ implies error amplification. The intermediate regime (SC $\sim$50--55\%) shows the only positive trends because the majority is not yet strong enough to dominate extraction. Whether 70B+ models or trained extractors shift the Pareto frontier is open.

\section{Analysis}
\label{sec:analysis}

The regime-dependent pattern in \S\ref{sec:main-results} establishes \emph{where} SICA succeeds and fails. This section investigates \emph{why}: trace correlation quantifies the SC plateau (\S\ref{sec:effective-k}), symbolic confirmation bias identifies the root cause (\S\ref{sec:confirmation-bias}), process-level independence reveals a deeper bottleneck (\S\ref{sec:process-kappa}), supporting diagnostics confirm the mechanism (\S\ref{sec:diagnostics}), and more than twenty remediation strategies demonstrate a fundamental independence-accuracy trade-off (\S\ref{sec:remediation}).

\subsection{Condorcet Effective-K}
\label{sec:effective-k}

Table~\ref{tab:independence} reports Fleiss' $\kappa$ and Effective-K (Eq.~\ref{eq:effk}) across 15 conditions at $K = 12$. Among instruction-tuned models, $\kappa$ ranges from 0.21 to 0.82, yielding $K_{\text{eff}} = 1.20\text{--}3.62$. The four Mistral-7B FOLIO seeds produce $\kappa \in [0.41, 0.51]$, yet $\Delta$ ranges from $+3.43$ to $-0.49$\,pp---seed-level constraint quality, not independence alone, appears to influence the variation. Two conditions are jointly necessary for positive $\Delta$: sufficient $K_{\text{eff}}$ ($\leq 1.30$ never improves) and sufficient SC accuracy ($K_{\text{eff}} = 3.62$ with SC $= 39\%$ produces significant degradation). Cross-model validation confirms universality: all four families produce $\kappa \geq 0.41$ (Table~\ref{tab:kappa_generalization}; Appendix~\ref{app:cross-model-kappa}).

